<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>He hath taken our sins away,</l><l>When on Calv’ry’s cross He bled;</l><l>The disease of our soul He heals</l><l>By His Spirit freely shed;</l><l>Though Satan hath pierced us deep,</l><l>And great the grace each prays;</l><l>The more we prove His might,</l><l>The Savior who saves always.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Long, alas! in the gloom I fought,</l><l>’Mid strife of wind and waves;</l><l>Jesus seemed only this to me:</l><l>A Savior who sometimes saves.</l><l>But sweet are the light and calm</l><l>That fill my happy days,</l><l>Since now I fully trust</l><l>The Savior who saves always.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>O my Sun and my Shield art Thou</l><l>Lead on where Thou hast trod;</l><l>My Salvation, my Joy, my Song,</l><l>My Brother, and yet my God.</l><l>Whate’er then my life betide,</l><l>I now can trust and praise;</l><l>Each moment Thou wilt save,</l><l>O Savior, who sav’st always.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
